# Each claim keeps one sense in every statement that uses it.
# Aquinas's reply distinguishes what is self-evident "in itself" from what is self-evident "to us". It also notes that not everyone understands "God" this way. Both points attack the premises (P3, A2). Neither shows a word changing sense between statements, so I name no bridge.
# The one candidate is A2. It moves from "understanding the word entails actual existence" to "known as soon as the terms are known". These are different claims, each in its own sense, so A2 is not a bridge.
